+Its support items project the same static role union used by the profile's raw
+validator: `realization`/`verifier_artifact` require a nonempty artifact path and
+null command ID; `verifier_execution` requires a nonempty command ID and null
+artifact path. Both closed object forms require a prior Result reference. The
+existing Valibot-to-JSON-Schema projection emits nested `anyOf` in the supported
+2020-12 dialect, with explicit field descriptions; it does not rely on prose to
+enforce the shape. This generic projection is composed into the consumer's
+installed schema, rather than hand-authored for a scenario. The binder then
+checks actual Result kind and selected file/command membership. No raw answer
+is normalized or stripped, and negative/indeterminate judgments may retain
+nonempty evidence. Schema/binder evidence must exercise those nonempty forms;
+empty support alone does not establish their correspondence.
